<!-- WHAT WE LOOK FOR -->
<section class="cx-section">
  <div class="cx-container">
    <div class="r">
      <div class="cx-eyebrow">What We Look For</div>
      <h2 class="cx-h2">The people who thrive<br>at VNG.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="cx-problem-grid stagger" style="margin-top:48px">

      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Project Managers</h3>
        <p>You have managed commercial interior renovations from permit to handoff. You can read a schedule, run a trade meeting, and write a change order without being walked through it. You know what permit-ready drawings look like and what sub-par ones cost you.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Site Supervisors</h3>
        <p>You know how to sequence trades. You are on site early, you know what is happening in every corner of the job, and you do not need to be told to book the rough-in inspection before drywall goes up. You protect the schedule.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Estimators</h3>
        <p>You can build a detailed commercial renovation estimate from drawings. You know what allowances hide and you refuse to quote on incomplete information. You understand the difference between a competitive bid and a buyout strategy.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="cx-problem-card r">
        <h3>Skilled Trades</h3>
        <p>Framers, drywallers, millwork installers, and flooring mechanics who work in commercial environments and meet commercial tolerances. You show up when scheduled, you clean up your work, and you coordinate with the other trades on site.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

